and any software code added in the future), unless a specific folder says
otherwise.

4. Definitions
Throughout this License, capitalized words have the exact meanings set forth
below:

- "Commercial Use": Any use of the Work, in whole or in part, directly or
  indirectly in or for a commercial business, revenue-generating activity,
  monetized product, paid support service, professional consulting engagement,
  managed service provider (MSP) offering, paid training, or any activity
  conducted to obtain commercial advantage or financial compensation.
  * Included Examples: Running the Work to protect paid subscribers of an ISP;
    selling an appliance containing the Work; providing paid consulting to
    deploy the Work; integrating the Work into a commercial SIEM.
  * Excluded Examples: Personal self-study on a home computer without financial
    gain; reading the research papers for unpaid academic learning.

- "Contribution": Any code, documentation, bug fix, patch, translation,
  enhancement, or other material submitted to the Licensor for inclusion in
  the Work by You.

- "Derivative Work": Any work, system, code, document, or publication that is
  based upon, adapted from, translated from, or substantially derived from the
  Work or any portion thereof, including republished structural summaries or
  competing system designs substantially copying the Work's architecture.

- "Licensor": Dhanush B S [OWNER LEGAL NAME TO CONFIRM], the individual copyright
  owner of the Work.

- "Operator": Any Internet Service Provider (ISP), telecommunications carrier,
  network operator, transit provider, or enterprise operating an autonomous
  system or broadband access infrastructure.

- "Permission": An explicit, written, signed or verifiable email approval
  granted directly by the Licensor to an identified individual or organization,
  specifying the exact permitted scope, territory, duration, and conditions.

- "Production Use": Any execution, deployment, or operation of the Work (or
  any derivative thereof) on any live computer network, router, switch, or
  system carrying real subscriber, user, or carrier traffic.

- "Research Materials": All technical dossiers, whitepapers, mathematical
  proofs, telemetry formulas, regulatory analyses, diagrams, and markdown
  files contained in the Work.

- "Software": Any computer code, scripts, daemons, algorithms, schemas, or
  executable instructions contained in the Work now or added in the future.

- "Work": The collective bundle of Research Materials, Software, and assets
  made available under this License.

- "You" (or "Your"): The individual or legal entity exercising any permission
  granted under this License.

In plain English:
These are the exact legal definitions used throughout the license so there is
no confusion about what words like "Commercial Use" or "Operator" mean.

