10. Prohibition on Commercial Use
You shall not engage in any Commercial Use of the Work, or any part thereof,
without prior written Permission from the Licensor.

In plain English:
No business, consultant, or company can use this work to make money or assist
their operations without written permission.

11. Prohibition on Republication and Redistribution
You shall not copy, mirror, republish, redistribute, sublicense, or sell the
Work, in whole or in substantial part, on any website, book, package, or
platform without prior written Permission from the Licensor.

In plain English:
You cannot copy-paste these research papers or code onto another website, blog,
or product without permission.

12. Prohibition on Derivative Works
You shall not adapt, translate, modify, build upon, or create Derivative Works
from the Work without prior written Permission from the Licensor.

In plain English:
You cannot modify these files or build a customized version without written
permission.

13. Prohibition on Competing Systems
You shall not use the architecture, formulas, disassemblies, or research
contained in the Work to design, develop, market, or operate a competing
commercial product or service.

In plain English:
You cannot read this research and use it to build a competing software product
to sell to ISPs.

Risk / Enforceability Note:
Under Indian and international copyright law, copyright protects the specific
"expression" of an idea, not the general idea, mathematical formula, or concept
itself (the Idea-Expression Dichotomy). While this clause contractually binds
those who agree to the License, stopping a third party who independently builds
a similar mathematical system from public RFCs is legally difficult without
patent protection.

14. Prohibition on Machine Learning and AI Training
[OPTIONAL - OWNER TO CONFIRM]
You shall not use the Work, including Research Materials, formulas, schemas,
and Software, to train, fine-tune, evaluate, or validate any artificial
intelligence, machine learning model, large language model (LLM), or automated
code generation system, nor include the Work in any dataset assembled for such
purposes, without prior written Permission from the Licensor.

In plain English:
Companies cannot feed this repository into AI training datasets without
explicit permission.

