D. CONDITIONS ON ANY PERMISSION GRANTED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

15. Specificity of Permission Grants
Any Permission granted by the Licensor must be in a formal written instrument
(or verified digital document) that expressly specifies:
(a) The legal name of the permitted individual or entity;
(b) The exact permitted scope and use case;
(c) The exact duration (time limit) of the grant; and
(d) The exact territory (geographical limit) of the grant.

In plain English:
Any permission must be in writing and must say exactly who gets it, for what,
for how long, and in which city or country.

Risk / Enforceability Note:
Under Section 19(5) of the Indian Copyright Act, 1957, if an assignment or
license does not state the duration, it is deemed to be 5 years. Under Section
19(6), if the territorial extent is not stated, it is deemed to apply only
within India. Setting duration and territory explicitly in every permission
letter prevents these default statutory rules from applying unexpectedly
[VERIFY Section 19 Copyright Act 1957].

16. Non-Transferability
Any Permission granted under this License is strictly personal to the named
recipient and cannot be assigned, transferred, or shared with any third party
without the prior written consent of the Licensor.

In plain English:
If you get permission, you cannot hand that permission over to someone else or
another company.

17. No Sublicensing
No recipient of Permission has any right to sublicense, lease, or grant
sub-permissions to any other person or organization.

In plain English:
You cannot give other people permission to use what you were permitted to use.

18. Attribution Requirement
Any permitted use, deployment, or display of the Work must prominently maintain
all copyright notices and include the credit: "ARCUS by ToxArch (Dhanush B S)".

In plain English:
Whenever you are permitted to use this, you must keep the original copyright
and creator credits visible.

19. Revocation for Cause
The Licensor reserves the right to revoke any Permission granted upon giving
fourteen (14) days [OWNER TO CONFIRM: 14 vs 30 days] written notice if You
breach any condition of the Permission or this License.

In plain English:
If you violate the terms of your permission, the owner can cancel your
permission after giving you a 14-day written warning.

20. Permission Application Process
To request Permission, applicants must email the Licensor at the official
contact address specified in Section 50, providing:
(a) Full legal name, address, and corporate registration details;
(b) Detailed technical description of intended use;
(c) Subscriber base size and network topology (for Operators);
(d) Target deployment territory and anticipated start date.
The Licensor reserves absolute discretion to approve, condition, or deny any
request without obligation to state reasons.

In plain English:
